WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.040 --> 00:00:05.580
Wade Wilson returns in Deadpool 2 for some
wicked jabs at Wolverine, Marvel and much

00:00:05.580 --> 00:00:09.340
more in a sequel that's chock full of easter
eggs, jokes and meta-moments.

00:00:09.340 --> 00:00:13.630
Yippee-ki-yay, movie lovers, it's Jan here
and today I'm breaking down the very best

00:00:13.630 --> 00:00:16.950
easter eggs and references you might have
missed in Deadpool 2.

00:00:16.950 --> 00:00:20.970
If you're finding me for the first time, do
subscribe to get all my new Deadpool and Marvel

00:00:20.970 --> 00:00:24.370
videos, plus I'm giving away some awesome
Deadpool 2 merch.

00:00:24.370 --> 00:00:25.990
More details on that later.

00:00:25.990 --> 00:00:30.119
Obviously, spoilers ahead for the movie, so
take care if you haven't seen it yet.

00:00:30.119 --> 00:00:34.770
Although Domino survives thanks to her power
of good luck, it's a bit of a shocking moment

00:00:34.770 --> 00:00:39.200
when Deadpool's new X-Force team barely lasts
a few minutes before getting dispatched in

00:00:39.200 --> 00:00:41.050
various gruesome ways.

00:00:41.050 --> 00:00:45.230
But the X-Force has already faced this kind
of bloodbath in the comics where in X-Force

00:00:45.230 --> 00:00:49.620
#116 almost all the members of a new X-Force
team were killed off in what was known as

00:00:49.620 --> 00:00:50.990
the Boyz 'R Us massacre.

00:00:50.990 --> 00:00:56.350
Part of the movie's X-Force team was the Vanisher
played by Brad Pitt who we only actually see

00:00:56.350 --> 00:01:00.920
in the film when his character's electrocuted
on power lines during a parachute jump.

00:01:00.920 --> 00:01:05.239
In the comics, the Vanisher's a teleporting
criminal though at one point he was forced

00:01:05.239 --> 00:01:07.260
to join the X-Force team.

00:01:07.260 --> 00:01:11.460
When Deadpool gets covered in ash during the
final fight, turning his red suit grey, that's

00:01:11.460 --> 00:01:14.660
a nod to his grey-coloured X-Force suit.

00:01:14.660 --> 00:01:19.030
Deadpool 2 reintroduces Juggernaut into the
X-Men movie world, with the villain having

00:01:19.030 --> 00:01:23.729
previously appeared in X-Men: The Last Stand
after which some of his lines were parodied

00:01:23.729 --> 00:01:25.909
becoming internet memes.

00:01:25.909 --> 00:01:30.390
Given that X-Men 3 was retconned away after
Days of Future Past created a new timeline,

00:01:30.390 --> 00:01:35.150
this is presumably a new and better Juggernaut
than Vinnie Jones's version.

00:01:35.150 --> 00:01:40.630
This time, Juggernaut is all CGI and his voice
is provided by Ryan Reynolds himself.

00:01:40.630 --> 00:01:44.690
In the movie, Deadpool is a huge fan of Juggernaut
and when he meets him, he rattles off some

00:01:44.690 --> 00:01:48.439
of his favourite comic book issues featuring
the unstoppable being.

00:01:48.439 --> 00:01:54.370
There's Uncanny X-Men #183, where Juggernaut,
aka Cain Marko, starts a bar brawl with Colossus.

00:01:54.370 --> 00:01:59.271
Then there's Thor 411 where Juggernaut is
taken to New York by Loki and ends up in a

00:01:59.271 --> 00:02:01.420
fight with the God of Thunder.

00:02:01.420 --> 00:02:06.310
And there's X-Men Unlimited 12 where Cain
Marko was trapped inside the Crimson Gem of

00:02:06.310 --> 00:02:07.619
Cyttorak.

00:02:07.619 --> 00:02:11.409
And although Juggernaut appears to be defeated
at the end of the film, having been electrocuted

00:02:11.409 --> 00:02:16.010
then shoved into a pool, if you watch the
final scene very carefully you'll notice Juggernaut

00:02:16.010 --> 00:02:20.779
is still alive moving around in the pool,
so it seems he shares his comic-book counterpart's

00:02:20.779 --> 00:02:22.970
power of near invulnerability.

00:02:22.970 --> 00:02:26.760
In Deadpool 2, Juggernaut also reveals that
he wears a helmet because his brother, who

00:02:26.760 --> 00:02:29.420
is in a wheelchair, tries to read his mind.

00:02:29.420 --> 00:02:32.980
This is a reference to Juggernaut's family
history in the comics where he's actually

00:02:32.980 --> 00:02:37.169
the step-brother of Professor X who, of course,
uses a wheelchair.

00:02:37.169 --> 00:02:41.620
Wade actually spends some time wheeling around
in that famous wheelchair at the X-Mansion.

00:02:41.620 --> 00:02:45.980
And there's a funny moment with Wade ranting
about the studio not giving Deadpool any top-tier

00:02:45.980 --> 00:02:47.390
X-Men characters for his movie.

00:02:47.390 --> 00:02:52.459
What Wade doesn't realise though is that just
behind him there's a room full of X-Men including

00:02:52.459 --> 00:02:57.959
Quicksilver, Cyclops, Nightcrawler, Professor
X and Beast who quietly closes the door on

00:02:57.959 --> 00:02:59.950
the Marvel motor-mouth.

00:02:59.950 --> 00:03:05.040
During his X-Men rant, Deadpool mentions the
one with "giant pigeon wings", likely a reference

00:03:05.040 --> 00:03:08.459
to Angel who worked for Apocalypse in the
previous X-Men movie.

00:03:08.459 --> 00:03:13.359
Later on, there's also an amusing scene of
Wade wearing Cerebro and pretending to know

00:03:13.359 --> 00:03:15.469
what Colossus is thinking.

00:03:15.469 --> 00:03:19.579
Deadpool jokes that it smells like Patrick
Stewart and also breaks Cerebro as he takes

00:03:19.579 --> 00:03:21.129
it off.

00:03:21.129 --> 00:03:24.920
Deadpool's rivalry with Wolverine and Hugh
Jackman continues in the sequel.

00:03:24.920 --> 00:03:29.031
The film begins with a musical figure of an
impaled Wolverine in a throwback to how he

00:03:29.031 --> 00:03:31.079
died at the end of Logan.

00:03:31.079 --> 00:03:35.189
Wade also complains about Logan copying Deadpool's
R-rating.

00:03:35.189 --> 00:03:38.670
The musical theme "Don't Be What They Made
You" from the Logan soundtrack that played

00:03:38.670 --> 00:03:43.719
when Logan died also plays in Deadpool 2 as
Deadpool tries to talk Firefist down from

00:03:43.719 --> 00:03:45.680
killing the Headmaster.

00:03:45.680 --> 00:03:49.650
And when Deadpool signs a packet of cornflakes
for a young kid that has Hugh Jackman's Wolverine

00:03:49.650 --> 00:03:54.819
on the packet, it could be a nod to Laura,
aka X-23, in the Logan movie.

00:03:54.819 --> 00:03:59.719
By the way, the child actor who plays the
kid with the cereal box in Deadpool 2 also

00:03:59.719 --> 00:04:04.939
appears in the TV show Legion as a young mutant
David Haller, whose father in the comics is

00:04:04.939 --> 00:04:06.319
Professor X.

00:04:06.319 --> 00:04:10.980
There's also another Hugh Jackman nod via
Deadpool's hand-drawn plan which features

00:04:10.980 --> 00:04:16.790
a picture of Wolverine in the DMC Prison with
the number 24601 above it.

00:04:16.790 --> 00:04:22.350
That was the same prisoner number that Jackman's
character Jean Valjean had in Les Miserables.

00:04:22.350 --> 00:04:26.840
Deadpool 2 doesn't really tackle Cable's mutant
origins, but there is a nice easter egg to

00:04:26.840 --> 00:04:31.250
his mother Madelyne Pryor via the Pryor's
Treats ice-cream van which pops up near the

00:04:31.250 --> 00:04:34.350
billboard where Deadpool lands with his parachute.

00:04:34.350 --> 00:04:38.540
Madelyne Pryor was a clone of Jean Grey and
was created by Mr Sinister with the aim of

00:04:38.540 --> 00:04:43.950
her having a child with Scott Summers aka
Cyclops so that Sinister could use their offspring

00:04:43.950 --> 00:04:45.810
as a weapon.

00:04:45.810 --> 00:04:51.300
Deadpool makes a joke about Cable's height
in the movie and how he's only 5 foot 11 – much

00:04:51.300 --> 00:04:55.120
shorter than in the comics where his height
is typically around 6 foot eight.

00:04:55.120 --> 00:04:56.120
"Sheriff Deadpool."

00:04:56.120 --> 00:04:57.880
"You know, you're a lot..."

00:04:57.880 --> 00:04:59.460
"Shut up you little..."

00:04:59.460 --> 00:05:03.370
And when Cable tells Deadpool, 'You're not
a hero, you're just an annoying clown dressed

00:05:03.370 --> 00:05:08.560
up as a sex toy', it's a hat-tip to Deadpool's
hatred of clowns in the comics, which was

00:05:08.560 --> 00:05:12.340
also referenced in the first movie during
his visit to the oncologist.

00:05:12.340 --> 00:05:16.540
Another Mr Sinister connection comes via the
Essex School for the Young, the institution

00:05:16.540 --> 00:05:19.380
where both Firefist and Domino were raised.

00:05:19.380 --> 00:05:24.040
Mr Sinister's real name is Nathanial Essex
and the supervillain was last teased in the

00:05:24.040 --> 00:05:28.570
X-Men: Apocalypse post-credits scene where
men working for Essex Corp entered the Weapon-X

00:05:28.570 --> 00:05:33.390
facility to collect vials of mutant blood
which likely also contained samples of Wolverine's

00:05:33.390 --> 00:05:34.390
blood.

00:05:34.390 --> 00:05:37.820
It'll be interesting to see whether Mr Sinister
is slowly being set up as a big bad for the

00:05:37.820 --> 00:05:39.950
whole of Fox's X-Men franchise.

00:05:39.950 --> 00:05:45.500
And the Essex School with its cult-like propaganda
and anti-mutant agenda feels reminiscent of

00:05:45.500 --> 00:05:47.460
the Purifiers in the comics.

00:05:47.460 --> 00:05:52.760
The Purifiers were set up by the fanatical
X-Men hater William Stryker and became a quasi-religious

00:05:52.760 --> 00:05:56.640
organisation that carried out terrorist attacks
on the mutant population.

00:05:56.640 --> 00:06:01.010
Amongst the propaganda at the school are banners
which say "M-Day is here".

00:06:01.010 --> 00:06:05.210
M-Day which was also known as the Decimation
is the Marvel Comics event in which Scarlet

00:06:05.210 --> 00:06:08.000
Witch depowered masses of mutants.

00:06:08.000 --> 00:06:12.510
And anti-mutant leaders like William Stryker
saw M-Day as a kind of divine signal to take

00:06:12.510 --> 00:06:16.390
further steps against the remaining mutant
population.

00:06:16.390 --> 00:06:20.610
Deadpool 2 also features tons of call-backs
to moments from the first Deadpool movie,

00:06:20.610 --> 00:06:25.010
but one especially interesting one is how
the sequel pays off a line Wade said to Blind

00:06:25.010 --> 00:06:26.610
Al in the 2016 film.

00:06:26.610 --> 00:06:30.210
"There's about 116 kilos of cocaine buried
somewhere in the apartment..."

00:06:30.210 --> 00:06:31.800
"Right next to the cure for blindness."

00:06:31.800 --> 00:06:33.100
"Good luck."

00:06:33.100 --> 00:06:36.871
And just as he promised, we see a package
labelled "Cure For Blindness" nestled among

00:06:36.871 --> 00:06:39.210
Wade's stash of coke in Deadpool 2.

00:06:39.210 --> 00:06:45.231
By the way, according to an EW interview with
Deadpool back in 2016, Codswallop, the last

00:06:45.231 --> 00:06:49.750
thing Deadpool says in the sequel just before
he dies, is his favourite word.

00:06:49.750 --> 00:06:54.160
Not only does Deadpool use the post-credits
scenes to go back and "fix the timeline" by

00:06:54.160 --> 00:06:59.280
shooting himself in X-Men Origins: Wolverine,
but he also pokes fun at another crazy scene

00:06:59.280 --> 00:07:00.560
in that movie.

00:07:00.560 --> 00:07:05.210
In Deadpool 2, during his fight with Cable
on board the convoy, Deadpool rapidly moves

00:07:05.210 --> 00:07:09.870
his katanas in an almost futile attempt to
block the bullets from Cable's guns, though

00:07:09.870 --> 00:07:14.620
he does manage to split one bullet in two,
as also happened in Origins: Wolverine.

00:07:14.620 --> 00:07:19.230
Of course, in the new film Wade ends up full
of bullet holes, unlike his alter-ego in Origins

00:07:19.230 --> 00:07:24.180
where the Merc with a Mouth miraculously deflected
a hail of incoming bullets as Team X entered

00:07:24.180 --> 00:07:27.430
the HQ of a diamond-smuggling operation.

00:07:27.430 --> 00:07:32.680
Also in the post-credits, Deadpool calls Negasonic
Teenage Warhead, Eleven, referencing El from

00:07:32.680 --> 00:07:37.640
Stranger Things whose extraordinary psychokinetic
abilities have been likened to Jean Grey,

00:07:37.640 --> 00:07:41.680
with Stranger Things itself having also made
numerous X-Men references on the show.

00:07:41.680 --> 00:07:45.840
After he's fitted with a power-suppressing
collar at the mutant prison, Deadpool pokes

00:07:45.840 --> 00:07:50.460
fun at the non-superpowered archer Clint Barton,
saying, "give me a bow and arrow and I'm basically

00:07:50.460 --> 00:07:51.669
Hawkeye".

00:07:51.669 --> 00:07:55.780
Deadpool also tries to calm down the enormous
Juggernaut using the same words that Black

00:07:55.780 --> 00:07:59.690
Widow used to talk the Hulk back down to being
Bruce Banner in the MCU

00:07:59.690 --> 00:08:01.460
"Hey big guy.

00:08:01.460 --> 00:08:03.820
Sun's getting real low."

00:08:03.820 --> 00:08:08.020
Of course, Deadpool's not the first to make
fun of that line from Age of Ultron; director

00:08:08.020 --> 00:08:11.430
Taika Waititi got there first in Thor: Ragnarok.

00:08:11.430 --> 00:08:17.230
Josh Brolin who plays Cable also plays Thanos
in the MCU and the Mad Titan gets a shout-out

00:08:17.230 --> 00:08:20.450
when Deadpool tells Cable, "Zip it, Thanos!"

00:08:20.450 --> 00:08:24.830
Deadpool also calls Cable an old grump with
a Winter Soldier arm, comparing him to the

00:08:24.830 --> 00:08:28.500
Marvel character Bucky, who also has a cybernetic
limb.

00:08:28.500 --> 00:08:32.620
And when the motor-mouthed merc finds out
that Cable's from the future, he asks the

00:08:32.620 --> 00:08:37.610
time-traveller: 'at what point do audiences
say, enough with the robotic arms?!'

00:08:37.610 --> 00:08:43.279
Just before his Basic Instinct parody, Deadpool
calls Domino "Black Black Widow" and towards

00:08:43.279 --> 00:08:46.200
the end of the movie, he calls Dopinder "Brown
Panther".

00:08:46.200 --> 00:08:50.809
Whether he's selling hot dogs on a beach,
listening to music in a library, or delivering

00:08:50.809 --> 00:08:56.209
packages to Tony Stank, Stan Lee's cameos
have become a highlight of many Marvel movies.

00:08:56.209 --> 00:09:00.140
In the first Deadpool film, Lee popped up
as a DJ at a strip club.

00:09:00.140 --> 00:09:03.899
At the time, Lee said that was his favourite
cameo, however, you won't see Stan the Man

00:09:03.899 --> 00:09:05.819
in person in Deadpool 2.

00:09:05.819 --> 00:09:10.660
Instead, this time his cameo is more akin
to his appearances in Netflix's various Marvel

00:09:10.660 --> 00:09:11.660
shows.

00:09:11.660 --> 00:09:16.010
So, look out for a big mural of Lee as Domino
parachutes into the city to intercept the

00:09:16.010 --> 00:09:18.639
convoy transporting Firefist.

00:09:18.639 --> 00:09:22.410
Also according to the screenwriters the statue
that Deadpool knocks over in the X-Mansion

00:09:22.410 --> 00:09:25.350
is a bust of Stan Lee as well.

00:09:25.350 --> 00:09:30.170
Captain Marvel's getting her debut solo movie
in the MCU next year and Deadpool 2 includes

00:09:30.170 --> 00:09:34.829
a sneaky nod to the "Alpha Flight" superhero
team which Carol Danvers recently led in Marvel

00:09:34.829 --> 00:09:35.829
Comics.

00:09:35.829 --> 00:09:40.519
The Alpha Flight easter egg appears on the
top of Dopinder's taxi as an ad for a Canadian

00:09:40.519 --> 00:09:43.610
airline offering cheap flights and travel
deals.

00:09:43.610 --> 00:09:47.910
Before Captain Marvel recently headed up the
team, Alpha Flight was a Canadian superhero

00:09:47.910 --> 00:09:54.699
team introduced in Uncanny X-Men #120 and
has had numerous members over the years including

00:09:54.699 --> 00:09:57.670
Wolverine, Guardian, Northstar, Aurora, and
Snowbird.

00:09:57.670 --> 00:10:01.889
Deadpool and Spider-Man have history in the
comics and the Merc with a Mouth sometimes

00:10:01.889 --> 00:10:06.371
even gets confused with the Wall-crawler due
to similarities in their outfits, so it's

00:10:06.371 --> 00:10:09.690
not surprising to find some Spidey nods in
Deadpool 2.

00:10:09.690 --> 00:10:13.889
First up, there's what looks like a Spider
symbol on one of the kitchen cabinets near

00:10:13.889 --> 00:10:16.269
the entrance to Wade and Vanessa's apartment.

00:10:16.269 --> 00:10:21.480
And just before Colossus goes up against Juggernaut,
Deadpool says, "go get 'em, tiger".

00:10:21.480 --> 00:10:26.440
Kirsten Dunst's MJ said those same words to
Tobey Maguire's Peter at the very end of Spider-Man

00:10:26.440 --> 00:10:31.629
2 and "Face it Tiger, you just hit the jackpot"
were Mary Jane's first words to Peter Parker

00:10:31.629 --> 00:10:32.629
in the comics.

00:10:32.629 --> 00:10:37.360
By the way, Kirsten Dunst also gets name-checked
for her role in the film Interview With A

00:10:37.360 --> 00:10:40.860
Vampire, which gets discussed by Dopinder
and Deadpool.

00:10:40.860 --> 00:10:44.850
Towards the start of the movie, after we've
watched Deadpool blast himself to smithereens

00:10:44.850 --> 00:10:50.139
and a montage of his numerous kills, the Merc
with a Mouth tells us that Deadpool 2 is actually

00:10:50.139 --> 00:10:55.069
a family film and, just like 'all good family
films', it starts with 'a vicious murder.'

00:10:55.069 --> 00:11:00.250
To prove his point, Deadpool name-checks two
animated Disney classics, Bambi and The Lion

00:11:00.250 --> 00:11:05.470
King, both of which feature early parental
deaths, and to hammer home the joke, Wade

00:11:05.470 --> 00:11:08.180
includes Saw 7 on his list of family films
as well!

00:11:08.180 --> 00:11:13.139
You'll hear the song 'Tomorrow' from the musical
Annie several times during Deadpool 2.

00:11:13.139 --> 00:11:18.500
This particular version is from a 1999 Disney
TV special of the famous musical about a young

00:11:18.500 --> 00:11:19.500
orphan.

00:11:19.500 --> 00:11:23.120
The song fits with Deadpool 2's idea that
"kids give us a chance to be better than we

00:11:23.120 --> 00:11:28.220
used to be", as Vanessa says, and given that
the song is all about optimism, it seems especially

00:11:28.220 --> 00:11:32.910
fitting that it plays during scenes with Cable
and his daughter, whose name is Hope.

00:11:32.910 --> 00:11:36.869
And "Tomorrow" also plays during the scene
where Deadpool sacrifices himself to save

00:11:36.869 --> 00:11:38.490
Firefist.

00:11:38.490 --> 00:11:42.019
Interestingly , there are a couple of viral
videos out there of Ryan Reynolds performing

00:11:42.019 --> 00:11:46.800
his own version of 'Tomorrow', one on a Korean
TV show and another in a birthday message

00:11:46.800 --> 00:11:48.449
with Hugh Jackman.

00:11:48.449 --> 00:11:52.629
Despite Vanessa's reassurances, Wade worries
that when they have children he'll be a bad

00:11:52.629 --> 00:11:53.660
father like his own dad.

00:11:53.660 --> 00:11:58.360
And he even cites Star Wars as evidence that
'men are destined to become their father,

00:11:58.360 --> 00:12:00.550
then have consensual sex with their sister.'

00:12:00.550 --> 00:12:04.769
Obviously, Wade's thinking of Luke and Darth
Vader's relationship, and of Luke kissing

00:12:04.769 --> 00:12:09.290
Leia, which Vanessa reminds him was actually
in The Empire Strikes Back.

00:12:09.290 --> 00:12:13.730
When Deadpool shows his hand-drawn plan to
his X-Force crew, you can see the words "pew

00:12:13.730 --> 00:12:18.079
pew" scrawled in crayon next to Cable's gun,
which is a hat-tip to the noise made by blasters

00:12:18.079 --> 00:12:20.319
in the Star Wars movies.

00:12:20.319 --> 00:12:24.220
Another Star Wars nod comes in the credits
where the actress who plays Yukio gets a note

00:12:24.220 --> 00:12:29.059
pointing out that "The X-Force is strong with
this one", perhaps suggesting that Yukio will

00:12:29.059 --> 00:12:30.600
be returning in the X-Force movie.

00:12:30.600 --> 00:12:36.149
There's a running joke about Disney Animation's
highest-grossing movie Frozen during Deadpool

00:12:36.149 --> 00:12:37.149
2.

00:12:37.149 --> 00:12:41.309
It starts off when Wade and Vanessa are watching
Barbra Streisand sing 'Papa, Can You Hear

00:12:41.309 --> 00:12:46.220
Me?' in the movie Yentl, and Wade asks, 'Does
this song sound familiar to you?'

00:12:46.220 --> 00:12:50.360
And it continues at Weasel's bar with Deadpool
asking, "Is it just me or does 'Do You Wanna

00:12:50.360 --> 00:12:51.360
Build A Snowman?'

00:12:51.360 --> 00:12:55.300
from Frozen sound suspiciously like 'Papa,
Can You Hear Me?' from Yentl?"

00:12:55.300 --> 00:12:58.889
Deadpool seems kind of annoyed about it, but
Dopinder loves Frozen.

00:12:58.889 --> 00:13:03.920
Alan Tudyk, who voices the Duke of Weselton
in the animated movie, makes a brief appearance

00:13:03.920 --> 00:13:09.800
in Deadpool 2 as Redneck #1 whose conversation
about toilet paper with another Redneck character,

00:13:09.800 --> 00:13:14.709
played by an unrecognisable Matt Damon, is
cut short when Cable arrives and takes their

00:13:14.709 --> 00:13:18.879
truck, a scene which has vibes of Terminator
2 where Arnold Schwarzenegger also robbed

00:13:18.879 --> 00:13:20.869
a vehicle from some rednecks.

00:13:20.869 --> 00:13:25.569
By the way, in real life, Barbra Streisand,
who co-wrote, directed and starred in Yentl,

00:13:25.569 --> 00:13:28.959
is the stepmother of Josh Brolin, Deadpool
2's Cable!

00:13:28.959 --> 00:13:33.579
Rob Liefeld, who co-created the comic-book
character Deadpool, got several name-checks

00:13:33.579 --> 00:13:35.420
in the first Deadpool movie.

00:13:35.420 --> 00:13:39.550
And Deadpool 2 continues the shout-outs, for
example, when Wade starts complaining about

00:13:39.550 --> 00:13:44.119
which comic book artist came up with a character
whose superpower is luck, he rants that it

00:13:44.119 --> 00:13:46.589
was probably someone who can't draw feet.

00:13:46.589 --> 00:13:52.230
Which is a wink at Liefeld's interesting perspective
on anatomy, especially feet, in his comic-book

00:13:52.230 --> 00:13:53.260
drawings.

00:13:53.260 --> 00:13:58.639
And when Cable turns up at Blind Al's apartment,
his utility belt draws some sarcastic remarks

00:13:58.639 --> 00:14:04.619
from Weasel, which is a reference to Liefeld's
trademark pouch-laden comic-book costumes.

00:14:04.619 --> 00:14:09.930
At the start of the film, Deadpool very deliberately
blows cigarette smoke towards the camera which

00:14:09.930 --> 00:14:15.110
could be a little dig at Disney who've banned
characters smoking in any PG-13 Disney film

00:14:15.110 --> 00:14:17.670
including Marvel, Star Wars and Pixar.

